KG42.register("clusters-37e94efccf93a78bd4dfd611",{"id":"08-real_time_prices::v142-d-CL002","paper":"08-real_time_prices","label":"TSO joint balancing optimization, real-time pricing, and signal publication","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-CL002","label":"TSO joint balancing optimization, real-time pricing, and signal publication","market_meaning":"Using day-ahead information, RP bids, operating states, and forecasts of wind power and aggregate response as inputs, the TSO selects regulation deployment and real-time prices or forecasts through a single-period or multi-period model, then publishes them according to the applicable timing. The supplied chains support a candidate assembly of this decision and delivery interface, but mathematical closure of the price response and some applicability conditions remain incomplete.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01","v141-a-M02"],"market_types":["DEM"],"process_stages":["clearing","coordination","bidding"],"scope_disposition":"unresolved","scope_explanation":"M01 and M02 are linked only through the interfaces for external RP bid inputs and submission deadlines, and DEM is retained as a frozen source label. The single-period and multi-period models are retained under their respective conditions. The five-minute architecture and model time step, as well as pre-regulation for future scenarios and the fallback condition in the absence of imbalance, have not yet been fully aligned; they cannot be interpreted as an unconditionally unified model, nor can the absence of RP bids be inferred from EcoGrid's bid-free participation.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"The decision inputs and optimization results of R003 have explicit information interfaces with the price outputs, forecasts, and publication activities of R004 and should jointly express the operator's pricing rules. R007 is shared only as an external bid interface; its independent bid-submission admission rules belong to v142-d-CL003. Participation eligibility and users' modes of autonomous response belong to v142-d-CL001.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R003","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides bid inputs, objectives and feasibility conditions, and regulation-deployment and price-decision objects; the single-period and multi-period schemes remain in the original chain."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R004","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides the relationship between optimized prices and coordination signals, conditional price rules, forecasts, and publication timing; procedural pricing statements are not treated as mathematically closed formulations."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R007","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"Provides context on the entities, sizes, and deadlines for external RP bids; the bid-size threshold is not rewritten as a lower bound on regulation deployment, nor are all RP entities mapped to generating units in the model."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-CON007","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev20","v141-b-g01-ev31"],"rationale":"The M02 source describes the RP bid entry point, while the M01 source explicitly states that the TSO uses upward and downward regulation bids submitted by generating units. The interface is limited to those generating-unit bids; the large consumers and aggregated loads in R007 are not thereby equated with the objects indexed by g in R003."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CON008","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-ev-07","v141-b-g01-ev30"],"rationale":"The corresponding sources for the two mechanisms describe the same RP bid-submission deadline arrangement; R004 additionally retains its temporal relationship with real-time signals within the operating hour. Only the interface scope is aligned here, without upgrading sequence to a new dependency edge or classifying the two complete constraints as duplicate expressions."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CON009","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C003","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C004"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C003","v141-c-R004::E::v141-c-R004-E002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-ev-17","v141-b-g02-ev-22"],"rationale":"The source explicitly uses single-period optimization for pricing in the next time step and multi-period optimization for the next-time-step price and forecasts for future scenarios. This reference identifies the source of the optimization described in R004, retaining the applicability conditions of both schemes without copying objectives or adding C scientific edges."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CON010","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-x-LAMBDAR"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R004::x::lambda_R"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev07","v141-b-g01-ev31","v141-b-g02-ev-17","v141-b-g02-ev-22"],"rationale":"The same mechanism delivers real-time prices or forecasts determined by optimization to market participants, thus connecting optimization quantities with coordination quantities. The actual signal for the next time step and forecasts for future scenarios remain distinguished according to their original stages; this interface does not establish that the currently frozen mathematics is sufficient to obtain prices."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM002","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::V::clearing.social_welfare","v141-c-R004::V::clearing.social_welfare"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R003::V::clearing.social_welfare","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-ev-17","v141-b-g02-ev-22"],"rationale":"The social-welfare optimization referenced by R004 is precisely the single-period or multi-period optimization function recorded separately in R003; R003 serves as the display representative, while all original node references and model conditions are retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM003","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-x-LAMBDAR","v141-c-R004::x::lambda_R"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev07","v141-b-g01-ev31","v141-b-g02-ev-17","v141-b-g02-ev-22"],"rationale":"The quantity definitions and output uses in the source jointly support the correspondence of the two objects to the same real-time price quantity; the basis is not merely identical symbols. The optimization-decision role, publication role, and scopes of applicability to the first stage and future scenarios are retained separately."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM004","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-theta-LAMBDA-D","v141-c-R004::theta::lambda_D"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev05","v141-b-g01-ev11","v141-b-g01-ev23"],"rationale":"Within the corresponding scope of the same operating hour, both reference the price given by the day-ahead market. The cost or response benchmark role in R003 remains separate from the fallback or planning signal role in R004; this mapping does not presume that prices in different hours are equal."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-GAP004","category":"math_incomplete","description":"R003 has not incorporated the price-response relationships from source Eqs. (8), (9), (20), and (21) into the existing constraints. Although real-time prices are listed as decision quantities, their mathematical linkage to response quantities has not been closed through the supplied main objective expression and feasibility constraints; the conditional fallback rule in R004 cannot complete the general pricing formulation.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003","v141-c-R004"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-x-LAMBDAR","v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-x-DPL","v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-x-DPDER","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C003","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C004","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C003","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C005"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-ev-20","v141-b-g02-ev-21","v141-b-g02-ev-25","v141-b-g02-ev-27"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g02-prop-01"],"required_work":"At the C layer, check and explicitly add source-supported response constraints and object bindings, distinguishing the next time step from future scenarios; D retains the gap and does not derive substitute price formulas."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-GAP005","category":"math_incomplete","description":"Eq. (2) contains LF_0, which has not been declared as an independent quantity object, and the t=0 quantities have not been clearly distinguished as fixed observed inputs. The total-output relationship is listed only in the domain of P^G, and clear constraint references and conventions for linking stages are still missing; the existing catalog cannot directly be regarded as a complete executable model.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C005","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C006","v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-x-PG"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev03","v141-b-g02-ev-12","v141-b-g02-ev-15","v141-b-g02-ev-19","v141-b-g02-ev-24"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"A subsequent version of C must declare source-supported initial inputs and index ranges and clarify how Eqs. (4), (15), and the existing domain are used as model constraints; D must not fabricate initial values or definitions that have not been supplied."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-GAP006","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"The following have not been aligned: V^{LOL}_{1} in Eqs. (3) and (14) with the parameter declared by l; α_{(d,1)} in the future DER term of Eq. (14) with the scenario coefficients; and the scenario-specific reference load and DER in Eq. (16) with parameters lacking s. Eq. (19) also references t=1,s output that is not explicitly connected to the common first stage. These differences cannot be eliminated by mapping quantities with the same name.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C003","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C004","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C006","v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-theta-VLOL","v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-theta-ALPHA-DER","v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-theta-PL","v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-theta-PDER","v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-x-PG"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev04","v141-b-g01-ev05","v141-b-g02-ev-18","v141-b-g02-ev-23","v141-b-g02-ev-24","v141-b-g02-ev-25"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check the transcription of the original text and the symbol definitions, then have the C layer explain the indices and scopes of applicability item by item or explicitly revise them; retain all original expressions in this round without selecting speculative corrections."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-GAP007","category":"scope_conflict","description":"R004 specifies a five-minute implementation, whereas R003 does not declare the model time step. UR_g and DR_g are labeled MW/h, but Eqs. (7) and (19) apply them directly to MW output bounds; Table I in B instead labels them MW/12min, and the multi-period numerical example also uses a twelve-minute time step. These three temporal specifications cannot be directly merged.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003","v141-c-R004"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-theta-UR","v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-theta-DR","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C005","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C006","v141-c-R004::theta::Delta_t","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C006"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev04","v141-b-g01-ev12","v141-b-g02-ev-19","v141-b-g02-ev-25","v141-b-g02-ev-28","v141-b-g02-ev-33"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the time steps and ramping units of the architecture, general model, and numerical example separately, and explicitly state time-conversion conventions at the C layer; do not directly substitute five-minute parameters into the twelve-minute numerical example or add multiplicative factors to the original equations."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-GAP008","category":"scope_conflict","description":"The condition for falling back to the day-ahead price in the absence of imbalance or congestion does not yet specify the time horizon over which it is assessed in multi-period pre-regulation. The numerical example in B allows current wind power to equal its expected value while pre-regulation for future scenarios causes price deviations; therefore, matching current wind power to its expected value alone cannot establish that the fallback condition holds. In addition, R003 provides no network-congestion constraints and cannot be considered to cover the entire congestion-pricing design in R004.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003","v141-c-R004"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C004","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C006","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C003","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C004","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C005"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev11","v141-b-g02-ev-22","v141-b-g02-ev-33","v141-b-g02-ev-34"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Clarify the system states and time horizon involved in the fallback condition, retaining the distinct scopes of applicability of single-period, multi-period, and congestion treatment; to cover congestion pricing, the upstream layer must supply source-supported constraints or continue to identify their absence explicitly."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-GAP009","category":"upstream_missing","description":"Successful pricing depends on the assumptions that aggregate response is predictable and that a certain response can be achieved through prices. R004 has recorded the ICT conditions, but the existing chains do not fully express the operating conditions for adaptive forecasting, rapid feedback, and compensation of forecast errors by RP; the shared bid-submission rules cannot complete this operational closed loop.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003","v141-c-R004"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-theta-ALPHA-L","v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-theta-ALPHA-DER","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C005","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C015"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev32","v141-b-g02-ev-16","v141-b-g02-ev-36","v141-b-g03-e08","v141-b-g03-e09"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g02-prop-01"],"required_work":"Subsequently, have the C layer supply source-supported premises concerning forecasting and response attainability and clarify the scope of responsibility for handling errors; maintain the distinction between TSO expectations and participants' actual performance obligations."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-GAP010","category":"ontology_extension","description":"The dedicated node proposals for regulating-power deployment, price-forecast publication, and the day-ahead benchmark price remain unapproved. Existing quantity objects and clearing and coordination nodes may be referenced, but this does not mean that these ontology extensions have been adopted or that actual deployment execution is already covered.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003","v141-c-R004"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-x-PGUR","v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-x-PGDR","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C010","v141-c-R004::theta::lambda_D"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev11","v141-b-g01-ev23","v141-b-g01-ev31","v141-b-g02-ev-22","v141-b-g03-e12"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g01-prop02","v141-b-g02-prop-02","v141-b-g03-prop-02","v141-b-g02-prop-03","v141-b-g01-prop04","v141-b-g03-prop-01"],"required_work":"Manually review the relevant concepts and the scope of duplicate proposals, decide whether to extend the ontology, and revise C separately; D does not insert new nodes or rewrite deployment as energy-trade execution."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-GAP011","category":"unverified_source","description":"All sources in this cluster remain unverified. Cross-mechanism interfaces use candidate evidence from their respective mechanisms, and mathematical and unit differences are identified solely from the supplied transcriptions; no independent conclusion on sources or scientific correctness has yet been reached.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003","v141-c-R004","v141-c-R007"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev05","v141-b-g01-ev07","v141-b-g01-ev20","v141-b-g01-ev30","v141-b-g01-ev31","v141-b-g02-ev-07","v141-b-g02-ev-17","v141-b-g02-ev-22","v141-b-g02-ev-23","v141-b-g02-ev-24","v141-b-g02-ev-25"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually examine source transcriptions, formula indices, units, and mechanism assignments, then examine all interfaces and gaps in this cluster; maintain candidate status and do not treat eligibility for experimental support as verification."}]},"rule_refs":["08-real_time_prices::v141-c-R003","08-real_time_prices::v141-c-R004","08-real_time_prices::v141-c-R007"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-334f35169e6933ed","COMP-42adfdfb6dfa84b0","COMP-5e870d267afec9a0","COMP-ab3d11c48c98c7be"]});
